{
  "title": "Open SaaS \u2014 SaaS (14,492\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Open SaaS\nDomain: SaaS | Scale: medium | Stars: 14,492\nProblem: Provides a free, open-source, feature-rich SaaS boilerplate that eliminates repetitive setup work for building production-ready SaaS applications with modern JavaScript technologies. Enables rapid SaaS development with built-in authentication, payments, email, and AI integration.\nTarget users: SaaS founders and developers, Startup teams, AI-assisted coding tool users, Full-stack JavaScript developers\nCore features: Multi-method Authentication (Email, Google, GitHub, Slack, Microsoft); Payment Integration (Stripe, Polar.sh, Lemon Squeezy); Email Sending (SendGrid, MailGun, SMTP); Background Jobs and Cron Tasks; AWS S3 File Upload Support; AI-Ready with Claude Code Plugin and Agent Skills; One-Command Deployment to Railway/Fly.io; ShadCN UI Components and Admin Dashboard\nIntegrations: Stripe, Polar.sh, Lemon Squeezy, SendGrid, MailGun, AWS S3, OpenAI API, Plausible Analytics, Google Analytics, Railway, Fly.io\nTech stack: React with ShadCN UI and Tailwind CSS + Node.js + PostgreSQL with Prisma ORM + Wasp full-stack framework, Railway/Fly.io deployment\nKey libraries: Wasp, Astro, Prisma, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Playwright, ESLint, Prettier\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Full-stack type safety is prioritized through Wasp's end-to-end type inference, eliminating redundant type definitions between frontend and backend\n- Extensive developer tooling (Prettier, ESLint, TypeScript) is built-in to maintain code quality at scale\n- AI-assisted development is a first-class citizen with dedicated documentation, plugins, and agent integration patterns\n- Deployment is abstracted through Wasp CLI to enable one-command deploys across multiple hosting providers",
